<urn:usf:currentness:semantic-first-bootstrap-transition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:deltaDigestScope> "Canonicalize every ordered operation kind, exact old and new N-Quad source line, subject, predicate, object, graph and expected preimage. Require exactly four resource additions and the two named state replacements, with no other source or semantic operation." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:currentness:semantic-first-bootstrap-transition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:postStateDigestScope> "At admission, apply the verified delta in memory and require exact equality of all three current post-state RealisationBasis values, source digest, six-resource projections, replacement postimages and the separately loaded core authority manifest/profile selection before writing or accepting the receipt. Preserve those exact member basis and scoped dependency digests as immutable admission evidence. Later permission currentness rederives the core authority semantic projection: exact source and reversible delta, authority manifest/profile/product/foundation identities and versions, directional digests, ordered work identities and work-resource digests, and the six admitted resource projections. Separately, post-closure stage currentness compares each checked member's exact basis and therefore its declared gate source, test, policy, schema, tool and preimage dependencies. Changed member dependencies make only that checked candidate stale and reconstructable; unrelated ANQR, provider-qualification, Hermes, recovery overlay or Git movement is outside this gate scope and does not force reproof." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:currentness:semantic-first-bootstrap-transition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:receiptExclusion> "The receipt is tracked evidence but is not imported by any semantic manifest. Its path and missing-file preimage are bound by the pre-state basis, while its expected creation is removed only from the unchanged-dependency comparison; its content bytes are excluded from the semantic delta and post-state semantic digests to avoid self-reference. Every closed field is independently recomputed, so changing, omitting or adding a field refuses rather than becoming authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:currentness:semantic-first-bootstrap-transition:1> <urn:usf:predicate:verificationOrder> "For admission, validate receipt schema and exact identities; reconstruct and verify pre-state; re-evaluate focused evidence and construction proof; verify and apply the exact reversible delta in memory; recompute and strictly compare all three post-state bases; then atomically write and read back source and receipt. For later permission checks, load the graph-declared core authority manifest/profile independently of any consumer profile and validate the immutable receipt, reversible source transition and exact scoped semantic post-state projection. For post-closure member stage, compare the current exact member basis with its immutable receipt basis; exact matches are checked-awaiting-integration, mismatches reconstruct under ordinary active permission, and neither state is completion." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
