<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-definition-activation-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-definition-activation-separation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Keep an authored SemanticContract definition distinct from proof-warranted RealisationPermission. A proofblocked definition grants no construction, contact, integration, publication, runtime or completion authority; only an exact typed BootstrapConstructionException may bound the one local isolated check-only gate construction." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-realisation-basis> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-realisation-basis> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive one immutable RealisationBasis binding exact manifest, profile, contract, permission, work packet, semantic trace, scoped dependency entries, write/preimage scope, evidence, proof, validation, policy, schema and tool digests. Reverify every slash-terminated directory dependency against its deterministic canonical source aggregate, expand it to the exact regular-file leaf path and digest closure, apply exact operation postimages to overlapping leaves and refuse missing, extra, modified, symlink or nonregular candidate entries. Candidate directory topology admits only ancestors of those authenticated regular source leaves and exact operation paths plus the one controlled .usf-check-tmp directory; an untracked empty source directory is neither copied nor semantic authority, while any extra candidate directory refuses. An exact operation beneath a slash-terminated write scope derives its file digest or null absent-file preimage only from that current reverified aggregate closure, then carries and rechecks that exact preimage like every other operation target; caller-authored child preimages grant no authority. The isolated publication-proof shadow expands the same exact authorized directory leaf closure before applying its tracked, ignored and secret-path screening per leaf, and copies only those admitted regular files. Use one owner-private, O_NOFOLLOW, nonblocking, process-released per-candidate util-linux advisory lock for each materialise/apply mutation and hold that same lock continuously from focused workspace cleanup and authentication through child exit." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-focused-network-confinement> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-focused-network-confinement> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Launch focused candidate and publication-shadow validation only through the exact trusted /usr/bin/bwrap host dependency with a new user, pid and network namespace, process-death release and an empty tmpfs root. Mount only explicit read-only /usr, /lib, /lib64, authenticated candidate workspace, node_modules and repository-local .usf/cache roots, a private proc and dev, and one read-write bind for the controlled scratch directory; host home, run, tmp, var-tmp and session sockets remain absent. Inside that boundary retain Node file, child-process and worker permission confinement and a cleared environment. Admit only the literal bounded graph command form node --test --test-isolation=none, one optional safe name pattern and repository-relative .test.ts paths; refuse eval, env-file, require, import, loader and every caller permission override before spawn. Missing or unsafe bwrap fails closed. One bounded in-child adversarial hook must machine-check denial of .env, .usf/home and historical-source reads, an outside-workspace write, an unapproved child spawn, a route and network request, and attempted secret-shaped canary exfiltration without weakening unrelated validation." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
