<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-construction-eligibility> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-construction-eligibility> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive ConstructionEligible per work item only from a complete current graph basis, declared applicability, exact stop/write boundaries and accepted prerequisites; dependency-ready alone is not semantic readiness." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-activation-eligibility> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-activation-eligibility> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive ActivationEligible only when exact admitted evidence satisfies every required evidence requirement and a deterministic current proof result passes for the exact obligation, algorithm/version and scoped basis; self-declared active state fails closed." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-transition-readback> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-transition-readback> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Route, call, resolve, apply and check must rederive or read back the same current RealisationBasis, refuse mixed or stale bases and preserve it in every result rather than trusting caller-supplied identities." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-transition-receipt-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-transition-receipt-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A self-closing admission must not hash itself into its own proof or become stale merely because its exact warranted mutation occurred. Use the closed external verified-transition receipt to bind reversible pre-state bytes and basis, the exact admitted delta and the exact expected post-state bytes and semantic projection; any other relevant movement invalidates activation. Every atomic source, receipt and recovery-journal temporary must write all intended bytes through a progress-checked loop, fsync, reread the exact size and digest through the same descriptor, and only then rename or link into place." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-work-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-work-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive verified-complete only from exactly one admitted post-integration receipt, one typed current Evidence and one typed current ProofResult for the exact work and its contract-declared completion obligations. The receipt binds the exact work, current RealisationBasis and scoped dependency digests, accepted candidate lineage and integrated byte-tree digests under a canonical receipt digest. Evidence and proof each bind that exact receipt and digest in addition to their current basis, evidence and passing algorithm bindings. Missing, ambiguous, stale, failed, sibling or aggregate construction records fail closed. Exclude completed work from ready results; every direct predecessor must be verified-complete and unrelated sibling completion is irrelevant." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-lifecycle-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-lifecycle-isolation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Process start may become ready and idle with no eligible work; proofblocked or stale work is excluded without blocking eligible siblings. Hermes may rank only the already eligible set and never defines evidence, proof or activation." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-nonserializing-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-nonserializing-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Cache eligibility and proof by exact scoped inputs, invalidate only affected work, and never reprove because of unrelated graph/product movement, provider retry, prompt iteration, lifecycle cycle or Git checkpoint." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-directional-basis> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-directional-basis> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Derive core-to-product and product-to-core content identities only through the exact profile-selected directional-currentness policy: hash the foundation plus selected non-product contract closure toward the product boundary, and hash the profile, product and selected product-contract closure toward the core boundary, carrying the opposite stable identity and version without its content so unrelated movement invalidates only the affected direction." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-first-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:requirement:semantic-first-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use one table-driven semantic eligibility test, one table-driven cross-transition basis test and one lifecycle sibling-isolation test; replace duplicate matrices rather than multiplying tests per command, provider, model or stage. The authoritative suite must pass against both the exact bootstrap pre-state and the exact verified post-state. A post-state is accepted only through its current closed transition receipt; any test needing a fresh pre-state must deterministically reverse that verified receipt's exact source operations rather than fabricate authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-order-topology> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-order-topology> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The exact seven-stage policy and graph-projected stop conditions are deterministic; missing, duplicated, unknown, skipped or code-invented stages fail closed." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-profile-selector> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-profile-selector> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The documented usf work selector accepts one exact graph-known RealisationProfile IRI directly, retains the explicit profile:IRI compatibility spelling, derives only that profile's closure and refuses unknown or malformed profiles; help and behavior must agree." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-eligibility-refusals> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-eligibility-refusals> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Missing evidence requirement, unresolved applicability, missing/failed/stale proof, proofblocked activation at a higher ceiling and relevant movement refuse while unrelated movement remains current." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-basis-integrity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-basis-integrity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Route through check preserves one exact current basis and refuses caller fabrication, mixed-basis contributions, stale preimages and policy/schema/tool mismatch before external contact or mutation. A graph-declared directory aggregate is reverified and expanded to exact candidate leaves; an exact directory candidate passes, while a changed leaf or missing, extra, symlink or nonregular entry refuses. Materialise, apply and focused execution use the same narrow per-candidate nonblocking advisory lock; a second cooperative operation refuses while execution holds it. Focused-check command arguments refuse every permission-affecting Node allow, no-allow, permission or no-permission spelling supported by the executing Node surface before spawn, including --no-permission; each admitted test path has canonical non-dot segments and resolves to a current regular non-symlink file contained by the authenticated candidate workspace; scrubbed NODE_OPTIONS grants no alternative. prepareFocusedCheck reports readiness only and never execution, checked status or authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-transition-receipt-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-transition-receipt-currentness> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The closed tracked receipt is outside semantic manifests, exactly reverses the current post-state to the proven pre-state, reproduces the exact admitted delta, requires strict equality of every post-state member basis at admission and preserves those bases as immutable evidence. Subsequent permission currentness refuses changed receipt, operation, semantic preimage or postimage, source, core authority selection, directional digest, ordered work resource, admitted resource or extra effect. Exact gate code, test, policy, schema, tool or preimage movement makes the affected checked member stale and reconstructable without treating it as completion or necessarily deactivating the permission; unrelated ANQR, provider-qualification, Hermes, recovery overlay or Git movement preserves the checked stage and does not trigger reproof." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-work-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-work-completion> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "The bootstrap aggregate transition activates construction only and leaves all three exact members checked-awaiting-integration. usf work --ready defaults to the construct stage; --ready --stage construct returns only construction-ready work and --ready --stage integrate returns only checked-awaiting-integration work. Evidence and proof without one exact admitted current integration receipt never complete work. A missing, ambiguous, stale or sibling receipt fails closed. Exact receipt-bound typed per-work Evidence and ProofResult mark that work verified-complete, exclude it from both ready stages and unlock a dependant only when every direct predecessor is complete." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-lifecycle-siblings> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:AcceptanceCriterion> <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
<urn:usf:acceptance:semantic-lifecycle-siblings> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A process is ready while proofblocked work is excluded, an eligible sibling progresses, affected movement invalidates only affected work and Hermes absence yields the same deterministic eligible plan." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
