<urn:usf:validation:realisation-basis-chain-focused> <urn:usf:predicate:admissionConfinementPolicy> "The outer self-admission proof grants no child-process permission. In that exact mode the integration fixture proves its graph/profile basis and leaves lock-owning preparation to this validation command's direct outer component execution; it does not recursively acquire candidate locks inside the no-child child. Outside the outer proof the same test invokes the real confined child check under the process-released per-candidate lock from controlled temporary cleanup and authentication through child exit. Before spawn, the command allowlist refuses every permission-affecting allow, no-allow, permission or no-permission argument spelling recognized by that Node runtime; the child receives only USF-injected read/write permissions, a scrubbed NODE_OPTIONS environment, a private route-free network namespace and the minimal explicit mount set. Lock-owning materialise/apply fixture cases run in the direct outer component validation and are not recursively re-executed inside that no-child candidate process; the nested check cannot gain child-process authority merely to retest its parent's lock boundary. Preparation never holds an execution lock and never returns checked status or authority." <urn:usf:graph:semantic-first> .
